    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0355" n="249" xml:id="pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00 Congress, Communist International, VII/63:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-21T19:00:00+03:00">August 21, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 21—3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>370. Personal for the President. I have just written an indecently long telegram
                    on the Communist Congress. I wish I could have talked with you, the Secretary,
                    Moore and Kelley instead. The main point is to handle the matter from the
                    domestic, not the foreign, political viewpoint. If by any chance you decide to
                    follow the line I have recommended, do have Kelley in on all drafting. The
                    technical complexities of Soviet organization are so great that his encyclopedic
                    knowledge will be indispensable. Whatever you do, the Bolsheviks will make it
                    hot for us here. But, as Judge Moore says, we are already accustomed to Hades
                    and acclimated. Love to your whole White House family and yourself.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
